Describe a time when you answer a phone call from someone you don't know in a public place.

I’d like to talk about a time when I answered a phone call from a stranger while I was in a café. This happened a few months ago when I was spending my weekend at a coffee shop near my workplace.

At that time, I was sitting by the window, drinking coffee and scrolling through my phone when I suddenly received a call from an unknown number. Normally, I don’t answer calls from strangers, but for some reason, I decided to pick it up because I thought it might be related to work.

The caller spoke in a very serious and professional tone and claimed to be from a bank. He told me there had been some suspicious activity on my account and said I needed to verify my information immediately to avoid losing money. Honestly, the way he talked sounded quite convincing at first, so I became a little nervous.

However, after a few minutes, I started to notice something strange. When I asked for his full name and the official contact information of the bank, he avoided answering directly and kept pressuring me to provide personal details. That was the moment I realized it was probably a scam call.

I immediately hung up and contacted my bank directly to check the situation. Fortunately, they confirmed that my account was completely safe and warned me that scam calls like this are becoming more common nowadays.

After the incident, I felt relieved but also a bit annoyed because it interrupted my relaxing afternoon. At the same time, it taught me to be more careful and never share personal information over the phone, especially with strangers.
